1079 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Yandex Cloud \050Data Engineer\051                                                         2025 \205 Present\n \nBuilt and operated multi\055stage production data pipelines across 8\053 business domains\054 processing terabyte\055scale data\073\nMigrated several of the largest production pipelines to PySpark for large\055scale distributed data processing\073\nLed migration of a core data model involving 100\053 dependent processes\054 improving performance and reducing operational complexity\073\nDesigned and maintained Data Quality monitoring and validation across production workflows\073\nOwned end\055to\055end incident resolution\054 including detection\054 root\055cause analysis\054 stakeholder communication\054 and permanent fixes\073\nContinuously optimized workflow performance and resource utilization\073\nCollaborated with engineering teams through technical troubleshooting and PR reviews\054 supporting engineering quality and maintainability\056\n\nLATOKEN \050Data Solutions Engineer\051                                             2023 \205 2025\n\nMaintained and optimized Airflow ETL pipelines processing more than 1 TB of production data per day\073\nDeveloped ingestion pipelines combining on\055chain and off\055chain data for 17k\053 tokens across 30\053 blockchain networks\054 increasing data coverage by 3x\073\nRedesigned DWH architecture together with 5 cross\055functional teams to improve scalability and query\055processing performance\073\nProcessed a 3 TB trading dataset using partitioned computation for Trading Desk PnL and analytical workloads\073\nBuilt 10\053 automated Power BI dashboards for operational monitoring\054 reconciliation\054 and business stakeholders\073\nTranslated loosely defined requirements into reliable production data solutions\056\n\nCloudReports \050Backend Developer\051                                              2021 \205 2023\n\nDeveloped ETL\057ELT integrations for 15\053 third\055party ERP\054 CRM\054 and marketplace APIs\054 delivering data into BigQuery and ClickHouse\073\nSupported 420\053 production integrations\054 handling pagination\054 rate limits\054 partial failures\054 late or restated data\054 and inconsistent vendor documentation\073\nDeveloped a reusable Python package that reduced development time for new integrations by 75\045\073\nCreated SQL views and data models to normalize integrated data for downstream analytics\073\nOptimized data export and processing logic\054 reducing Google Cloud resource costs by more than 5x\073\nWorked directly with clients and external data providers to translate inconsistent source systems and business requirements into reliable integration solutions\056)
     /K [ 13 ]
     /P 1080 0 R
     /Pg 1053 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
